.TH "HOMELAB-POWER" "1" "2026-11-06" "Homelab ops"
.SH NAME
homelab-power \- Control or query the selected host through the existing power-management route.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B homelab-power
[arguments]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Control or query the selected host through the existing power-management route.
Established names and consumer paths are preserved. No hardware or service action was executed for documentation verification.
.SH INTERFACE
.SS /usr/local/bin/homelab-power
Source: shared/scripts/power
.nf
p.add_argument('host',choices=['nexus','tensor','qubit'])
p.add_argument('action',nargs='?',choices=['on','off','status'])
p.add_argument('--via',choices=['nexus','tensor'],help='Awake LAN relay for magic packets')
.fi

.SH DEPENDENCIES
Use the interpreter in the source shebang and the existing host packages and services referenced in that source. Host configuration and private credentials remain on their original host.
.SH OPERATIONS
Before changing behavior, inspect inventory/audit-2026-11-06/nexus.json for recorded consumers and the source above for exact dependency paths. Never invoke a power, desktop, network, credential, notification, or storage operation merely to test it.
.SH SOURCE
Private iragonforce/ops repository. Consult docs/workflow.md for deployment, verification, rollback, and change records.
